= Evaluation

The developed methods will be evaluated using a range of anomaly detection, embedding-space, and computational performance metrics.

Anomaly detection performance will be evaluated using:

- AUROC
- AUPRC
- F-beta Scores (depending on the wanted balance between precision and recall)
- Confusion Matrix Metrics (Precision, Recall, Accuracy, and False Positive Rate)

Embedding-space quality will be evaluated using:

- Silhouette Score
- Intra-Cluster Distance
- Inter-Cluster Distance

Where appropriate, computational performance will also be considered, including:

- Embedding extraction time
- Inference time
- Memory requirements

Comparisons will be performed between global, local, and hybrid approaches to determine which representation provides the best balance between anomaly detection performance, interpretability, and computational efficiency.
